// Records the demo take: CL listing cold open -> paste into the app -> beats
// stream in the thread -> cursor tours the evidence panel -> hold on the read.
// Output: demo/out/take-<n>.webm (+ .mp4 via ffmpeg). Repeatable; iterate freely.
//
// take-12: beats run on an absolute schedule anchored at recording start,
// keyed to the edited narration (demo/narration-take8-edit.m4a: hesitations
// and one flub cut from the 2026-07-08 read; first word = video 0:00, last
// word 74.1s). Requires a warm cache: every lookup
// must land within ~2s of go or the tour clicks sections that aren't in yet.
import { chromium } from "playwright";
import fs from "fs";
import { execSync } from "child_process";
import ffmpeg from "ffmpeg-static";

// same URL the replayed scan-events.ndjson was recorded from, so the pasted
// link and the panel header agree; the ad page itself redirects to chicago.*
const LISTING = "https://www.craigslist.org/view/d/chicago-ft2-remodeled-studio-green/h9XWvsLpfZ51QVTtFURPVU";
const APP = process.env.DEMO_APP || "http://localhost:8123";
const OUT = new URL("./out/", import.meta.url).pathname;
const W = 1920, H = 1080;
const K4 = !!process.env.DEMO_4K; // capture at 2x device pixels, 3840x2160

// ---- injected cursor: macOS-style arrow, rAF bezier glide, click pulse ----
const CURSOR_JS = `
(() => {
  if (window.__demoCursor) return;
  const c = document.createElement("div");
  c.id = "__demo_cursor";
  c.innerHTML = '<svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="filter:drop-shadow(0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.4))"><path d="M5 2 L5 19 L9.5 15.5 L12.5 22 L15 21 L12 14.5 L18 14.5 Z" fill="#1a1a1a" stroke="#fff" stroke-width="1.4"/></svg>';
  Object.assign(c.style, { position: "fixed", left: "0px", top: "0px", zIndex: 2147483647, pointerEvents: "none", willChange: "transform" });
  document.documentElement.appendChild(c);
  let cx = innerWidth * 0.7, cy = innerHeight * 0.85;
  const put = (x, y) => { c.style.transform = "translate(" + x + "px," + y + "px)"; cx = x; cy = y; };
  put(cx, cy);
  window.__demoCursor = { x: () => cx, y: () => cy };
  window.__glide = (tx, ty, ms) => new Promise(done => {
    const sx = cx, sy = cy, dx = tx - sx, dy = ty - sy;
    const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dy) || 1;
    // control point perpendicular to the path: a slight human arc
    const mx = sx + dx / 2 - dy / dist * dist * 0.08;
# Narration — take-9 audio, edited cut (narration-take9-edit.m4a, 70.45s)

Recorded 2026-07-08 (raw: ~/Downloads/Untitled.m4a, 166s — three aborted
takes, the real one starts 87.6s in). The edit trims to the real take, then
inserts two room-tone gaps to sync with the hand-recorded screen capture
(~/Downloads/Built-in Retina Display.mp4, 70.45s): +1.0s before "You paste
the link" and +0.5s before the Zillow line. Gain +7.5 dB (the raw take sat
at -23.2 LUFS), limited to -2.0 dBTP → -16.0 LUFS. Total exactly 70.45s =
the video's length; 0.5s room-tone fade at the end.

Final: out/take-13-final.mp4 (video stream-copied from the screen
recording, narration muxed). Verified: "removed in 2017" lands on the
cursor highlight at 31-33s; "count the names" lands on the Names-we-found
table.

| Start | Line |
|-------|------|
| 0.0 | Say you're apartment hunting in Chicago and you find this studio for 865 a month. |
| 3.8 | It looks normal. There's a phone number and it says to call and ask for May. |
| 7.5 | At Autumn, we built a free listing investigator for exactly this. |
| 12.2 | You paste the link and every lookup fires at once. |
| 15.6 | The price, the property record, the phone, the photos, and even who's on public record at that address. |
| 20.2 | This one is 45% below the fair market rent for that area. |
| 26.6 | And the Zillow record here isn't even a rental. |
| 29.5 | The last event on it is the listing being removed in 2017. |
| 34.0 | And on the map, that's the Craigslist pin and that's where the Zillow record actually sits. |
| 39.8 | The phone's an internet line and it traces to Mika Ogiwara in Schaumburg. |
| 45.8 | And the photos turn up a second Craigslist post for the same unit. |
| 49.9 | So count the names. The ad says May, the phone says Mika, and on record at the address, Ora Grayson. |
| 56.2 | Autumn researched her too. Her LinkedIn says accounting, not real estate. |
